## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of zero-trust, cross-tenant governance, and service mesh integration in Azure for multi-tenant SaaS with minimal network churn. It probes practical decisions around identity, cryptography, and policy enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Azure AD workload identity for Kubernetes
- Istio mTLS and certificate management
- Private Endpoints for data plane isolation
- ABAC with policy-based access control
- Azure Policy and Lighthouse for cross-tenant governance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: validate that a service has a binding token from AD and that mTLS certs are valid
async function authorizeCall(service, peer) {
  const token = await fetchAzureAdToken(service);
  const cert = await getMTLSCert(peer);
  if (!token || !verifyCert(cert)) throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  if (!policyAllows(service, peer)) throw new Error('Policy denied');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and alert on policy violations across tenants?
- What rollback criteria would you implement for a failed rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical crypto hygiene, CMEK provisioning, tenant isolation, and operations around rotating keys without service downtime.

## Key Concepts

- CMEK per tenant with Azure Key Vault
- Encryption at rest for Cosmos DB with CMEK
- Per-tenant Managed Identities and RBAC
- Key rotation automation and rollback
- Policy and monitoring integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: create a CMEK and tie to Cosmos DB per tenant
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { KeyClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-keys");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const keyClient = new KeyClient(`https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net`, credential);
await keyClient.createKey("cosmos-cmek-tenantA", "RSA" );
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation without impacting customers?
- How do you handle key compromise or vault access revocation?

## Why This Is Asked
